tency":52.3,"_gate_incr_roic":0.06062752038333413,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":36.9,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.4152055508327758,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":100.0,"_gate_pool_share":0.21973544185960603,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.06905317232880295,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.12061211141201955,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.023491720700831584,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":60.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.00614,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":4.1,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Essential Properties Realty Trust, Inc. is an internally managed REIT that acquires, owns and manages primarily single-tenant properties that are net leased on a long-term basis to companies operating service-oriented or experience-based businesses. As of September 30, 2025, the Company's portfolio consisted of 2,266 freestanding net lease properties with a weighted average lease term of 14.4 years and a weighted average rent coverage ratio of 3.6x. In addition, as of September 30, 2025, the Company's portfolio was 99.8% leased to tenants operating 645 different concepts across 48 states. The company was founded in 2016 and is headquartered in Princeton, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Peter M. Mavoides | CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $2.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 56 people. Revenue per employee of $10.0M ranks in the top quartile among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 29%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $235K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Essential Properties Realty Tru is a mid-cap real estate business with a $6.1B market cap on $561M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +25% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage runs at 3.3\u00d7.","Net dilution runs at 6.9% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 3.2\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 94% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.937167741928513},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 42% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Growing faster than most Real Estate peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Liquidity Mapping Around (EPRT) Price Events","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/35/Liquidity_Mapping_Around_EPRT_Price_Events_111126124202_1794375722.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794375722.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Essential Properties Realty Trust (EPRT) Stock May Be Below Fair Value On Fresh Notes Pricing","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-eprt/essential-properties-realty-trust/news/essential-properties-realty-trust-eprt-stock-may-be-below-fa","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794122455.761,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.973,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Essential Properties Realty Trust, Inc. $EPRT Shares Bought by Sumitomo Mitsui Trust Group Inc.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/essential-properties-realty-trust-inc-eprt-shares-bought-by-sumitomo-mitsui-trust-group-inc.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793960003.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.976,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Do Options Traders Know Something About EPRT Stock We Don't?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3020690/do-options-traders-know-something-about-eprt-stock-we-don-t?cid=CS-ZC-FT-tale_of_the_tape%7Coptions-3020690","date":"2026-11-02